An archive stores one kind of item. Compare these proposed contracts:

```csharp
// A
interface IArchive<T>
{
    void Save(T item);
    T Load(string key);
}

// B
interface IArchive
{
    void Save(object item);
    object Load(string key);
}
```

An application needs an archive of `Invoice` objects. Explain how A preserves the intended contract when saving and loading, and what responsibility B leaves to runtime checks or caller casts. Use an attempt to save a `TemperatureReading` as a concrete example.
